Subject: Re: [CorpLing with R] A foundational question
Message-ID: <6KpnD-Xk4yo.PPJ5FUufqVAJ@corpling-with-r.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <6KpnD-Xk4yo.SZc03CFyoIAJ@corpling-with-r.groups.google.com>
References: <6KpnD-Xk4yo.SZc03CFyoIAJ@corpling-with-r.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/corpling-with-r/c/6KpnD-Xk4yo/m/PPJ5FUufqVAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

by pointing out that one is doing a SYNCHRONIC study where the object
of study is the population at a particular point in time (namely the
point in time the sample is representative for as opposed to a
diachronic one where the focus is precisely the flux you mention?

